  <!-- Research Direction -->
  <section class="section" id="research">
    <div class="section-label">Research Problem</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Why This Research Question?</h2>
    <div class="research-grid">
      <div class="research-card">
        <div class="card-label">Observation</div>
        <h3>Structural Gap in AI Doctoral Training</h3>
        <p>AI evolves monthly, but doctoral training cycles span years. Doctoral students master model accuracy — yet lack project delivery, team collaboration, and cross-domain transfer competencies demanded by industry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="research-card">
        <div class="card-label">Discovery</div>
        <h3>Hidden Growth in Experiential Learning</h3>
        <p>AI research environments — experimental iterations, open-source contributions, conference deadlines, team collaborations — inherently provide rich competency development opportunities. Yet they lack <strong>intentional design</strong>: growth happens by accident, not system.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="research-card">
        <div class="card-label">Framework</div>
        <h3>Introducing the CORE Framework</h3>
        <p>Rooted in CBE and Kolb's experiential learning theory, CORE reframes research projects as structured competency development contexts — helping AI doctoral students <strong>deliberately</strong> construct professional competencies alongside academic output.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="research-card">
        <div class="card-label">Value</div>
        <h3>Transferable & Verifiable</h3>
        <p>While AI doctoral students are the primary application context, CORE's logic transfers to engineering, data science, and other research-intensive disciplines. The framework includes operationalized competency definitions, reflection protocols, and assessment tools.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CORE Framework -->
  <div class="framework-section">
    <div class="framework-inner" id="framework">
      <div class="section-label">Theoretical Framework</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">CORE — Competency-Oriented Research Education</h2>
      <div class="core-intro">
        <div class="core-acronym">CORE</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Making Research Projects the Vehicle for Competency Development</h3>
          <p>CORE integrates Competency-Based Education (CBE) with Kolb's Experiential Learning Theory. Through four coordinated components, it helps doctoral students develop professional competencies beyond academic skills while conducting research. Core logic: embedding Kolb's experiential cycle into project structure — so every experimental iteration becomes a complete learning cycle: concrete experience → reflection → conceptualization → application.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="core-pillars">
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-icon">🧭</div>
          <h4>Competency<br>Definition & Mapping</h4>
          <p>Six competency domains: disciplinary knowledge, research methods, collaborative practice, self-management, reflective practice, professional communication</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-icon">🔩</div>
          <h4>Structured<br>Project Experience</h4>
          <p>Collaborative project structures, iterative planning & review cycles, delivery-oriented outcomes — projects as designed learning contexts</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-icon">🔄</div>
          <h4>Reflective<br>Practice Structures</h4>
          <p>Structured reflection protocols, regular reviews, peer reflection — converting tacit experience into visible competency growth</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-icon">📊</div>
          <h4>Assessment<br>& Feedback</h4>
          <p>Competency self-assessment tools, mentor feedback, portfolio documentation — making competency development visible, assessable, and trackable</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Background -->
  <section class="section" id="background">
    <div class="section-label">Background</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Research Questions Born from Practice</h2>

    <div class="bg-intro">
      <div>
        <h3>Insights from 9 Years of Project Management</h3>
        <p>Working at Beijing Zhongguancun Academy & AI Research Institute — where the mission is "breaking boundaries" and "project-based training with end-in-mind" — gives me direct access to the doctoral student population at the heart of both my research and their model. From research PM (2021 Shanghai Hollywave) to AI projects (2023 Sixents/NavInfo), to deep engagement with doctoral students (2025 Zhongguancun Academy) — This is something no research paper can replicate: <strong>first-hand observation of the gap</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stats-row">
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-num">9+</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Years PM Experience</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-num">30+</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Enterprise Projects Delivered</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-num">2</div>
          <div class="stat-label">AI Project Engagements</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="bg-col-header">
          <span style="font-size:20px;">🎓</span>
          <h3>Education</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline">
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="year">2018.09 — 2020.11</div>
